e\",\n                \"mainEntity\": [\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"What is Quickler?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"Quickler is a field compliance platform for UK and global trades firms that collects inspection and safety data from engineers via WhatsApp. Responses are processed automatically to produce PDF reports or dashboard records, removing the need for paper forms or separate apps.\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"How does Quickler work?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"Quickler sends a structured set of questions to an engineer's WhatsApp at a scheduled time or on demand. The engineer replies to each question on site, attaches photos where needed, and Quickler processes those responses into a formatted compliance record automatically. No data entry is required from office staff.\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"Who is Quickler for?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"Quickler is built for UK and global trades and inspection businesses whose field staff work on site — including M&E contractors, safety inspectors, structural engineers, and van fleet operators. It suits any firm that currently relies on paper forms, email attachments, or manual checklists to capture compliance data from site.\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"Does Quickler work through WhatsApp?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"Yes. Engineers interact with Quickler entirely through WhatsApp — there is no app to download, no login to remember, and no new interface to learn. Because WhatsApp is already on their phone, adoption requires no training.\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"What does Quickler produce at the end of a workflow?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"Completed workflows produce a timestamped, auditable record — either a formatted PDF report or a structured entry on the manager dashboard, depending on the workflow type. Records are available immediately once the engineer submits, with any flagged faults highlighted automatically.\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"Is Quickler only available in the UK?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"No. Quickler works anywhere WhatsApp does. The product is country-agnostic by design: a field worker answers questions on WhatsApp, adds photos, and Quickler produces a structured PDF report and dashboard record. None of that depends on a local app store, phone network, or national regulator. Quickler has deep roots in UK compliance frameworks such as EICR, CP12 and van safety checks, and the same workflow engine builds inspection and safety reports for firms outside the UK and across Europe and the United States. You can upload any inspection form, in any country, and Quickler will run it as a WhatsApp workflow. Pricing is available in GBP, EUR and USD, and data is hosted on EU servers (Hetzner, Germany).\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"Do engineers need training to use Quickler?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"No. Because Quickler uses WhatsApp — an app engineers already have and use daily — there is no onboarding process, no separate login, and no interface to learn. Engineers simply reply to messages as they would any other WhatsApp conversation.\"\n                        }\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                        \"name\": \"How is compliance data stored in Quickler?\",\n                        \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                            \"text\": \"All responses, photos, and generated reports are stored securely and linked to the relevant engineer, job, and date. Managers access records through the Quickler web dashboard. Data is retained in accordance with UK data protection law.\"\n                        }\n                    }\n                ]\n            },\n            {\n                \"@type\": \"ItemList\",\n                \"name\": \"quickler use case pages\",\n                \"itemListElement\": [\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n                        \"position\": 1,\n                        \"url\": \"https://quickler.co/pages/what-is-quickler.html\",\n                        \"name\": \"What is Quickler?\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                        \"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n                        \"position\": 2,\n                        